course: dictionary
lesson: 6878
title: Overlord and the power of rulers
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: An overlord is a ruler who has power over other rulers or lords. The word is made of two parts: over, meaning above, and lord, meaning a ruler. So an overlord is the lord who stands above the others. «Danylo still had to accept the Mongols as his overlords.» The clue is the word masters in brackets: the Mongols were the masters, and Danylo had to obey them.
explain: In history lessons about the Middle Ages, a great king or lord was the overlord of smaller lords. In return for land, the smaller lords promised loyalty and soldiers. This system is called feudal. «Moscow was a small principality, a land ruled by a prince, under the overlordship of the Golden Horde.» Overlordship is the power an overlord has, so Moscow's prince had to follow the Golden Horde.
explain: Stories and films often have an evil overlord who rules a land cruelly. People also use the word as a joke, like «our cat is the overlord of this house». Here the cat is not really a ruler, but it acts as if it owns the place. When you meet overlord, ask yourself: is this real history, a story, or a joke? The clues around the word will tell you.
fact: An overlord is a ruler with power over other rulers or lords.
fact: The word overlord is made of over and lord.
fact: «Overlordship» is the power an overlord has over others.
fact: A «principality» is a land ruled by a prince.
fact: «Tribute» is a yearly payment that a ruled land makes to its overlord.
fact: The Golden Horde was an overlord of Moscow in 1337, and Ivan III stopped paying it tribute in 1480.
exercise: In a history lesson, a king was the overlord of smaller lords. What did the smaller lords promise in return for land? | Their castles to the king's cat | Gold coins every single day | *Loyalty and soldiers
exercise: «Ivan III stopped paying tribute to the Horde.» What is tribute? | *A yearly payment to a ruler | A song sung at a party | A prize for winning a race
exercise: A joke says «our cat is the overlord of this house». What is the joke? | The cat is a real king who lives in a castle | The cat has lost its home | *The cat acts as if it rules the house
test: «Moscow was a small principality, a land ruled by a prince, under the overlordship of the Golden Horde.» What does overlordship mean? | A feast held by princes | A kind of royal crown | *Power and control over another ruler
test: What is a principality? | A giant castle | *A land ruled by a prince | A kind of horse | A type of tax
exam: Which word means a ruler who has power over other rulers or lords? | Peasant | *Overlord | Castle | Harvest
